+  - small SVG or PNG histograms.
+- A NEW test file, `test/salary-audit.test.js`. For every confirmed defect, write a test that fails now, named with its ID: SA-1, SA-2 and so on, numbered from 1. Use `test.todo`-style skipping only the way earlier audit tests do; read test/beta-data-check-3.test.js for the pattern. Also write pinned tests for behaviour that is correct.
+- Fixes. The backend engineer (`salary-audit-backend`) owns `server/normalize.js`, `server/salary.js`, `server/sources/*.js` except google.js, and `scripts/snapshot.js` / `scripts/build-static.js` for this work. Write your proposed fixes as patches in `docs/process/patches/salary-audit-data-*.diff`, and message them, by SendMessage to the agent doing `salary-audit-backend`, through the lead if you cannot reach them. server/sources/google.js belongs to a separate Google-grouping lane; for a Google salary bug, send a patch.
+
+**Rules:**
+- Don't commit and never push. Report with SHAs only if the lead asks; otherwise leave your changes uncommitted in your worktree and list the files.
+- No `pkill -f` / `pgrep -f`; use pid files.
+- Never `playwright install`; Chromium is at /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome with NODE_PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/pw/node_modules.
+- If the harness blocks you from writing a report-style Markdown file, return its full text in your final report, and the lead will write it. Never use a .txt workaround.
+- The user's standing rules: never cut or drop postings ("we must present them as they are and not cut anything"); don't change crawl request rates.
+
